.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-MEASURE-HOST 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-measure-host
.Nd record exploratory host lifecycle measurements
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3
.Ar scripts/measure-host-runtime.py
.Op Fl Fl output-root Ar directory
.Nm python3 scripts/measure-host-runtime.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3 scripts/measure-host-runtime.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run exploratory, instrumented workloads with one or eight trusted Python child
processes on a POSIX host with Python 3.10 or newer.
Start from the repository
root with the offline standards files already present.
The command uses the
host adapter's readiness, stop and reclamation paths, not host services or a
native Aether guest.
No root privileges are required.
.Pp
The runner checks three offline standards pins before workloads.
Each workload
runs two retained warmups and ten measured repetitions, sequentially, with a
fresh interpreter and private working directory per repetition.
A worker has
a 20-second outer watchdog.
A final silent-readiness control must spawn a child
and then hit its one-second watchdog; it is failure-control evidence, not a
latency sample.
Owned process-group teardown applies to non-detaching fixtures.
.Pp
Measurements cover construction, start-to-observed-readiness,
stop-to-reclamation,
total workload time, manager and reaped-child CPU, traced manager allocation
and the observed child count plus manager.
The waiting coordinator is excluded.
Timing uses perf_counter_ns; CPU uses getrusage user-plus-system deltas.
Tracemalloc is enabled throughout every worker measurement.
Memory excludes
imports, interpreter RSS and child memory.
Warmups do not control host caches,
frequency, affinity or other workstation activity.
.Pp
Summaries report median, nearest-rank p95 and maximum of successful measured
samples.
With ten samples p95 is the maximum.
Failures and warmups remain
recorded; unsuccessful runs cannot become fast samples or passing results.
These observations do not establish production thresholds or comparative
speed.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl output-root Ar directory
Parent for a new private run-* directory.
Missing parent directories are
created.
The default is out/host-measurements under the repository root.
Existing run directories are not reused or removed.
Relative paths resolve
from the caller's working directory.
Retain the complete result directory.
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without creating a run or launching workloads.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the measurement-command version and exit.
It is not a published release.
.El
.Pp
Hidden --worker, --directory and --stall options are internal control modes.
Worker count is restricted to 1 or 8 and requires a directory.
Directory or
stall without worker is invalid.
These are not workload customization options.
.Sh OUTPUT
Standard output contains a JSON summary with schema
sys-init-host-measurements-v1, result and the absolute results.json path.
Progress is written to standard error.
The report retains exact commands,
host/Python identity, selected source hashes, instrumentation, checks, raw
samples, failures, timeout-control results and summaries.
.Pp
A report starts in running state.
Only a completed pass is success.
Failed or interrupted attempts remain evidence.
Source drift prevents success.
Abrupt interruption or filesystem failure can leave a running or missing
report.
There is no automatic retry, evidence deletion or tool installation.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The invoking Python environment is inherited.
Child checks receive
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 through the aggregate runner's helper.
The worker passes AETHER_READY_FD to its own fixture child as part of the
host adapter protocol; users should not configure that descriptor themselves.
Load and host metadata are recorded, not stabilized by this runner.
.Sh FILES
.Pa out/host-measurements/run-*/results.json
contains the complete attempt.
Adjacent per-check stdout/stderr logs and
per-repetition directories preserve raw evidence, including spawned.json.
The selected source files and docs/*.lock are fingerprinted before and after.
This is a scoped input record, not complete system dependency closure.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
All required repetitions, checks and the timeout control passed and source
identities remained unchanged; also help and version.
.It 1
The final report failed, or an ordinary interpreter/infrastructure error
occurred.
.It 64
Invalid arguments or invalid internal option combinations.
.It 130
An interruption was caught while waiting for a child check; an interrupted
report is retained and later work stops.
.El
.Pp
An interruption elsewhere may leave a running report and does not guarantee
this caught-interruption exit path.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the repository root on the provisioned POSIX development host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/measure-host-runtime.py --help
python3 scripts/measure-host-runtime.py
.Ed
.Pp
The first command prints usage and exits zero without running fixtures.
The second creates a fresh run directory and executes all repetitions and the
expected timeout control.
Expect a JSON pass summary and exit zero on success;
retain all logs on failure.
This command is separate from functional check-all.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository guides: docs/HOST-MEASUREMENTS.md, docs/HOST-RUNTIME.md,
docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
.Sh CAVEATS
The manual title is not an installed executable.
Independent review and target
lookup remain pending.
These host observations are not a native init benchmark.
